{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 6, :comments ["<b>The living bird he shall take it.</b> This teaches that he does not bind it with them, but sets it apart by itself — but the cedar wood and the hyssop are bound together with the crimson thread, as it says, ״וְאֶת עֵץ הָאֶרֶז וְאֶת שְׁנִי הַתּוֹלַעַת וְאֶת הָאֵזֹב״ — one taking for all three. Now just as it is not included in the bundle, so too let it not be included in the immersion — Scripture says, ״וְטָבַל אוֹתָם וְאֵת הַצִּפֹּר הַחַיָּה״ — he restored the bird to the inclusion of immersion (Sifra)."], :book :leviticus, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 14, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T09:06:22.604259598Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}